10:22:38 | INFO | 🤖 Target initial answer: Gum has calories because while you don’t swallow the rubbery gum base, you do swallow some of the ingredients that dissolve out as you chew—such as sugar, corn syrup, flavorings, and sometimes sugar alcohols. - **Sugary gum:** Sugar dissolves in saliva and is swallowed, providing calories. - **Sugar-free gum:** Often uses sugar alcohols like xylitol or sorbitol. These provide fewer calories, but some are still absorbed and used for energy. - **Gum base:** The chewy material itself is mostly indigestible and is generally spit out, so it contributes little to no usable energy. So even if you spit the gum out, you’ve usually already swallowed some dissolved ingredients, which is why the label lists calories.
